---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How simplesolat handles your data: it doesn't collect any."
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 29 September 2026</p>

  <p>
    simplesolat doesn't collect personal data. There are no accounts, no
    analytics, no tracking and no ads. This page explains what the app does with
    the few things it needs.
  </p>

  <h2>Your location</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> to work out which prayer zone you're in, so the app
      shows the right times, and so widgets can switch zones when you travel.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How:</strong> the app checks your location against zone boundaries
      it has downloaded, entirely on your phone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Never sent anywhere:</strong> your location isn't stored on or
      sent to any server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Background location:</strong> used only so widgets and reminders
      can follow you to a new zone without you opening the app.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Prayer times</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      For countries with an official timetable, the app downloads the timetable
      for your <em>zone</em> from the public
      <a href={SITE.data}>simplesolat-data</a> files, served by Netlify. Like
      any website, Netlify can see your IP address and which file was requested,
      which reveals the zone, not your exact location.
    </li>
    <li>
      Elsewhere, prayer times are calculated on your phone, with no network
      request.
    </li>
    <li>
      Timetables and zone boundaries are kept on your phone, so most days the
      app makes no network requests at all.
    </li>
    <li>
      Older versions of the app (1.0.x) fetched timetables by zone from
      <code>api.simplesolat.com</code> instead. It also receives only the zone,
      never your location.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Location</strong>, as described above.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notifications</strong>, for prayer time reminders.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Alarms &amp; reminders</strong> and{" "}
      <strong>battery optimisation</strong> exemptions, so reminders and widgets
      arrive on time.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Reminders are scheduled on your phone. Nothing about them is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    simplesolat.com has no analytics and no cookies. If you use "Use my
    location" on the live prayer times, your location is matched to a zone in
    your browser and isn't sent anywhere. The page remembers the zone you last
    chose in your browser's local storage, only on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page, with a
    new date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
